# 1-bed / 1-bath cottage — the smallest complete plan.
# Open living+kitchen up front; a short 4 ft hall buffers the bedroom and bath.
# The bath's door sits at the far end of the hall so the corridor terminates at a
# doorway, not a blank wall. Exterior dims are on the 3 ft build module, and a
# back door off the kitchen gives the cottage a second way out.
plan "Stillwater Cottage"
envelope 33 x 24
ceiling 9
program 1 bed 1 bath

room living:  living   at 0,0    size 18 x 14
room kitchen: kitchen  north-of living size 18 x 10
room hall:    hallway  at 18,0   size 4 x 24
room bed:     bedroom  at 22,0   size 11 x 12
room closet:  closet   north-of bed size 11 x 3
room bath:    bathroom at 22,15  size 11 x 9

open living - kitchen width 8
door living - hall width 3 offset 0.5
door hall - bed width 3 offset 0.5
door hall - bath width 2.67 offset 5.83
# The closet is a 3 ft reach-in — a bifold centred on it keeps the whole rod
# within arm's reach (a person-door at one end would strand 8 ft of closet).
door bed - closet bifold width 8 offset 1.5

entry living south width 3 offset 13
entry kitchen west width 3 offset 3

# Covered landings at both exterior doors — a floor to step onto (IRC R311.3).
porch front at 11,-6 size 7 x 6 covered
porch side at -5,15 size 5 x 7 covered
window living south width 8 offset 2
window kitchen north width 6 offset 6
window bed  south width 4 offset 3
window bath north width 3 offset 4

# Smoke alarms: one in the bedroom, one in the hall outside it (IRC R314).
alarm smoke in bed
alarm smoke in hall
